# SECURESHRP.vec -- OVMX's SECURESHRP.EXE vector image: the rights-database
# services an image LINKed on real OpenVMS Alpha calls through SECURESHRP
# rather than SYS$PUBLIC_VECTORS (rd vms-8b5). SINGLE SOURCE for this image's
# symbol vector; format as in SYS$PUBLIC_VECTORS.vec. Clean-room: every offset
# is OBSERVED in the link map of our own rights probe, LINKed on the lab
# OpenVMS Alpha V8.4 node (tests/native-images/alpha/sp/SP_RIGHTS.MAP.txt);
# nothing comes from a VSI/HPE binary or source.
#
# Targets: $ADD_IDENT takes its name as a VMS descriptor, so it goes to the
# upper-case VMS-ABI entry point (src/vmsrms/rights_vmsabi.c);
# $CREATE_USER_PROFILE (0xE0, observed in SP_CHKPRO.MAP.txt and in
# docs/oracle/alpha84-symvec-offsets.txt) takes a descriptor and an item list,
# so it goes to src/libvms/syssvc/sys_vmsabi.c. Every other
# argument here is an identifier value or the address of a longword or of the
# holder quadword, the same layout for a 32-bit-pointer caller, so those slots
# name OVMX's own service (src/vmsrms/rightslist_live.c).
#
# GSMATCH: the probe recorded SECURESHRP ident major 1, minor 4, match LEQUAL
# (observed in its image section synopsis), so OVMX's carries 1,4.
#
#   gsmatch LEQUAL,1,4
#   use     LIBVMS$SHR.EXE
#   use     LIBVMSRMS$SHR.EXE
#
# offset  universal        OVMX target
0x000     SYS$ADD_HOLDER   sys$add_holder
0x010     SYS$ADD_IDENT    SYS$ADD_IDENT
0x030     SYS$FIND_HELD    sys$find_held
0x040     SYS$FIND_HOLDER  sys$find_holder
0x070     SYS$REM_HOLDER   sys$rem_holder
0x080     SYS$REM_IDENT    sys$rem_ident
0x0E0     SYS$CREATE_USER_PROFILE SYS$CREATE_USER_PROFILE
